{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure","id":584654,"title":"Developing Demonic Infrastructure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-09T06:55:15-07:00","id":584654,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Developing Demonic Infrastructure","content":"So here's my idea: what if <i>both</i> sides had infrastructure? Only the Demiurge can devise occult-matrices, however, meaning demons create infrastructure for the benefits said-constructs usually possess on their own.<br /> <br /> That raises another idea: should we design a system of for developing demonic infrastructure? Maybe something like the Zero-sum mechanic that's used when designing Pacts. Eg, the trickier it is is to build, the lower the cost gets, while the more beneficial it is, as well as how easy to detect and/or guard, raises the cost. And maybe that's just for the blueprint. You still need to get everything into place, which could be a whole chronicle in and of itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-09T08:09:47-07:00","id":584749,"title":"","content":"Possible effects:<br /> <br /> <b>Concealment</b><br /> Renders demons invisible to mortal scrutiny while they're within range<br /> Amplifies certain forms of Cover against compromise checks, even when obvious supernatural effects are present<br /> <br /> <b>Defense</b><br /> Acts as a stronghold against angelic invasion, with built-in wards, cryptid mooks, or even hellfire technology<br /> Forms an underground radio network warning of impending assault by enemy factions or angelic forces<br /> Endows a designated guardian with direct access to Aether/faith so long as their intentions are in defense against hostiles<br /> <br /> <b>Elimination</b><br /> Pending...<br /> <br /> <b>Logistical</b><br /> Spawns demonic cryptids allied to whomever controls the hive<br /> Acts as a forge/foundry for developing new gadgets and weaponry<br /> Help sustain and supply other forms of infrastructure allied with the owner<br /> <br /> <b>Command &amp; Control</b><br /> Influences popular trends or opinions on specific topics within local area<br /> Houses a demiplane aligned to its owner's faction","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 07-09-2015, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T05:51:44-07:00","id":604626,"title":"","content":"Guys? Anyone? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T06:49:47-07:00","id":604667,"title":"","content":"That sounds like a good idea but demons work by taking over infrastructure because occult matrix is much to hard for any to understand. Maybe you could change it to demons taking it over and then changing them over time studying a single infrastructure","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T09:29:16-07:00","id":604766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=604667#post604667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That sounds like a good idea but demons work by taking over infrastructure because occult matrix is much to hard for any to understand. Maybe you could change it to demons taking it over and then changing them over time studying a single infrastructure</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Would that influence cosmetic features?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T09:58:51-07:00","id":604784,"title":"","content":"Most likely demons could change it when they are working on causing it to look different also. Also remember that there maybe even more types of infrastructure out there.<br /> <br /> So your &quot;<b>Concealment</b><br /> Renders demons invisible to mortal scrutiny while they're within range<br /> Amplifies certain forms of Cover against compromise checks, even when obvious supernatural effects are present&quot;<br /> <br /> Could do things other then you stated maybe there is a concealment infrastructure that makes people not want to notice violence like a huge version of the bystander affect. <br /> <br /> Also the way it looks cosmetically when changed I guess would depend on the demons working on it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T10:12:27-07:00","id":604790,"title":"","content":"To be frank, I think such powerful resources would detract thematically from the game and cause fridge logic. Why bother with Agendas, Cults and the like when you can devote yourself 24/7 for a relatively long while to build the ultimate Fuck Off Already Infrastructure, forever eliminating the need to worry about anything? You wouldn't bother.<br /> <br /> That being said, if you really, really want to put this in your game, I suggest portraying this like the Token Maker Merit from 1st edition Changeling (Rites Of Spring). Something like 1 in hundreds of Demons have this Merit, and it might take <i>years </i>to build the Shiny Mighty Thing (unless you dump all your GMC Experiences into Primum, Crafts, Science etc). Oh, and you have to spend 1/3 of <i>all </i>your free time on the project, with only short pauses allowed if you don't want the Shiny Mighty Thing to become a Rusty Puny Thing. Teamwork rolls might be allowed if you manage to gather a bunch of Demons with this hypothetical Infrastructure Engineer Merit. The sum of costs should be daunting enough to explain why there are no Demonic Fortresses (that the Agendas know of). Searching for ways to speed up and streamline the engineering of Demonic Infrastructure would certainly make for long lasting story material. And if the players do find these miraculous blueprints of metascientific power, what then? It would be like playing the government of a nation with nukes, but it's probably more like a few Demons instead of a complicated web of geopolitics (at least before other Rings figure out how you did it).<br /> <br /> And being frank one more time, I would be lying my ass off if I said that the idea of a Rank 6 Angel being obliterated by a <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/WaveMotionGun\" target=\"_blank\">Hellfire Motion Gun</a> isn't a wet dream for Saboteurs.<br /> <br /> EDIT: the use of expletives and the like is for comical purposes, not a personal attack.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":4443,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","user":"GibberingEloquence","date":". 07-27-2015, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T10:46:08-07:00","id":604808,"title":"","content":"Honestly, in a very real way, Demons already have Infrastructure. They're called gadgets - and lambda can produce some very powerful, God-Machine level effects. Pacts are used to create new Covers. The big difference is that Gadgets don't produce aether from essence... which is something I don't think demons should be able to create on their own. Having to risk the G-M for access to that energy is a big thing in the game. <br /> <br /> As well, the five types of Infrastructure kinda work as an angelic equivalent to Agenda - the angelic mission they were assigned, instead of the demonic philosophy they chose to take up. The type of Infrastructure has nothing to do with the abilities - we have Destroyer, Guardian, Messengers, Psychopomps and likely Analysts in each and every type of Infrastructure, each with a different focus. Its all about the job the angels are given, what their focus is. <br /> <br /> I guess my point is that we already have demonic equivalents for most of the angelic stuff in the rules. What exactly do you want to do with demonic infrastructure that we can't already do? I mean, just looking over the ideas presented, I immediately see:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=584749#post584749\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Concealment</b><br /> Renders demons invisible to mortal scrutiny while they're within range<br /> Amplifies certain forms of Cover against compromise checks, even when obvious supernatural effects are present</div> </div> </div> </div> \u200bWe can make a multi-person gadget that works off making everyone invisible - there's one for using 4 Minutes Ago on an entire ring, after all. And we've a couple Embeds and Exploits for boosting compromise check chances. Turn them into a gadget, and voila.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Defense</b><br /> Acts as a stronghold against angelic invasion, with built-in wards, cryptid mooks, or even hellfire technology<br /> Forms an underground radio network warning of impending assault by enemy factions or angelic forces<br /> Endows a designated guardian with direct access to Aether/faith so long as their intentions are in defense against hostiles </div> </div> </div> I'm going to come out and say that the stronghold is a bolthole. This is exactly the kind of thing that Safe Place variants are made to deal with. Want better wards? There's plenty of ways to make a Gadget with Hellfire and a shotgun, then rig it up to the door. Underground radio network? That's one of the sample Free Agencies right there. Create a designated guardian - that's effectively a cryptid, enhanced stigmatic, or nephilim hooked up to an aether source, and its easy to make a pair of powerful batteries out of an Apple Watch and smart phone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Logistical</b><br /> Spawns demonic cryptids allied to whomever controls the hive<br /> Acts as a forge/foundry for developing new gadgets and weaponry<br /> Help sustain and supply other forms of infrastructure allied with the owner </div> </div> </div> Demonic cryptids are made via the Hellhound Exploit. We have rules for how to make forges already. Unchained use Pacts to help with creating new kinds of Covers and Gadgets as it is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>Command &amp; Control</b><br /> Influences popular trends or opinions on specific topics within local area<br /> Houses a demiplane aligned to its owner's faction </div> </div> </div> Fairly sure we have Vocal Embeds for making popular memes of choice go viral. As for demiplanes? That's literally what boltholes are for.<br /> <br /> <br /> Everything you suggested is part of the game already. It feels like we're just reinventing the wheel here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T11:05:09-07:00","id":604840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=604808#post604808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Everything you suggested is part of the game already. It feels like we're just reinventing the wheel here.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree, and I should have said this. Well observed, MCN. However, I do like the idea of Demons engaging in full blown Cold War style conflicts in search of the secret knowledge necessary to subjugate their designated enemies. Sure, if Demonic Fortresses become a trend, you are probably about to make it NWOD Unveiled. The God-Machine could also reduce you and your accomplices to homogeneous dust piles of fundamental particles before such plans are completed. The ramifications of these types of developments are fun to think about for people like me, that's all.<br /> <br /> Maybe a version of the NWOD that's been hollowed out by a horizon-breaking Demonic Fortress is locked away in the God-Machine's Apocalypse Vault?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T11:26:05-07:00","id":604877,"title":"","content":"Eh, I'm not interested in items so much as actual buildings. Otherwise, yeah, I'd just make a gadget. I'm talking about facilities that're more exposed than boltholes, but capable of being used in a... <i>turf war</i> scenario. More creative options for influencing territory, and the like.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=604808#post604808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to come out and say that the stronghold is a bolthole. This is exactly the kind of thing that Safe Place variants are made to deal with. Want better wards? There's plenty of ways to make a Gadget with Hellfire and a shotgun, then rig it up to the door. Underground radio network? That's one of the sample Free Agencies right there. Create a designated guardian - that's effectively a cryptid, enhanced stigmatic, or nephilim hooked up to an aether source, and its easy to make a pair of powerful batteries out of an Apple Watch and smart phone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Too basic. Need something with more flare.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 07-27-2015, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T11:37:19-07:00","id":604883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=604877#post604877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Too basic. Need something with more flare.</div> </div> </div> </div> I <b><i>was</i> </b>referring to buildings. I guess that should have been explicit in my post. And you know what? Challenge accepted. I'll return in the near future with a draft for a modified, spiffier Bolthole Merit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T12:22:26-07:00","id":604899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=604877#post604877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, I'm not interested in items so much as actual buildings. Otherwise, yeah, I'd just make a gadget. I'm talking about facilities that're more exposed than boltholes, but capable of being used in a... <i>turf war</i> scenario. More creative options for influencing territory, and the like.</div> </div> </div> </div> No one said that buildings couldn't be gadgets as well.<br /> <br /> The problem with something with &quot;more flare&quot; and used in a turf war is that DtD isn't exactly built for it. DtD is a spy game, where the assumption is that, if you go toe to toe, you'll be crushed. You're insurgents fighting against a massive, fully trained mililtary with nuclear options. Making a major base is a very good way for the superior forces to launch the equivalent of massive drone strikes against you and lay it to waste. So, the game is designed around being small and mobile, with guerrilla style tactics. <br /> <br /> That doesn't mean you can't go big. Its just not the default assumption. Easy enough to tweak bolt hole's fluff to be a bigger and badder Safe Place. Already comes with wards. Combined with Safe Place, it deals damage, grants bonuses, holds weapons. Hells, you can make a giant Safe Place with the occasional Bolthole as panic rooms. Ward the sucker, build some lambda that affect the entire area, use Hellhound and adopt some demon-kids, and you're good to go. You'll have everything you could need for a fortress. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Too basic. Need something with more flare </div> </div> </div> Define &quot;basic&quot; and &quot;flare.&quot; Without using any changes to the rules or setting, I've designed a Tempter palace for a local agency to live in comfort, as well as free to relax in their demon forms and generally free from Compromise checks, complete with stuff from Hiers to Hell, demon made cryptids, and Unchained guards armed with the best gadgets. <br /> <br /> And, to be honest, Infrastructure is actually pretty basic, when you get down to it. In mage terms, Infrastructure is nothing more than the <i>yantra</i> (people, place, time, items) used by the God-Machine for its spell (aka occult matrix).<br /> <br /> All in all, its pretty easy to make it more complex and flashier; just do the same thing the G-M does and add more levels to it. The problem is that its not spy-like (see above). If you don't mind the change in feel, then go ahead.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2102,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","user":"MCN","date":". 07-27-2015, 04:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T13:01:47-07:00","id":604913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=604899#post604899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No one said that buildings couldn't be gadgets as well.<br /> <br /> The problem with something with &quot;more flare&quot; and used in a turf war is that DtD isn't exactly built for it. Its not very spy-like, and, with the default setting, you'd be noticed. So, for that reason, DtD stuff is deliberately kept small and hidden. If you're changing things up a bit to make it a bit flashier, then it makes more sense to just adapt existing stuff instead of something new. All you need to do is tweak the Bolthole fluff to make them line up better, and combine them with Safe Place, and maybe other Safe Place merits from other lines.<br /> <br /> Define &quot;basic&quot; and &quot;flare.&quot; Without using any changes to the rules or setting, I've designed a Tempter palace for a local agency to live in comfort, as well as free to relax in their demon forms and generally free from Compromise checks, complete with stuff from Hiers to Hell, demon made cryptids, and Unchained guards armed with the best gadgets.<br /> <br /> And, to be honest, Infrastructure is actually pretty basic, when you get down to it. In mage terms, Infrastructure is nothing more than the <i>yantra</i> (people, place, time, items) used by the God-Machine for its spell (aka occult matrix). It just seems grander because the G-M has multiple layers, redundancies, and backup plans.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm getting the feeling you don't like me very much.<br /> <br /> As it stands, a game of spy vs spy isn't limited to a cell or even an agency. In the Cold War, America and the Soviet Union were very much aware of each other, and where their borders were, yet ultimately the threat of &quot;nuclear annihilation&quot;, as someone aptly put, meant only a shadow war could be introduced. And as the World of Darkness already shows numerous times, you don't need to be a Guardian of the Veil to fight a war mortals don't know about. Mages and Werewolves cause dramatic effects all the time without the world knowing they exist--mostly because of a cleanup crew, or cosmic shinanigans.<br /> <br /> Spy-like? A Summer Courtier would call it an option, but not the full spectrum of what war entails. We'd be bored if everyone played spies. I know, I've <i>played</i> that game on TF2... yick.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 07-27-2015, 04:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T13:33:12-07:00","id":604924,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=604913#post604913\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm getting the feeling you don't like me very much.</div> </div> </div> </div> Like doesn't enter into it. I've never attacked you personally, I'm just pointing out flaws in your arguments. I do that with everyone. Really, now. This is just unnecessary.<br /> <br /> &quot;I want to build Infrastructure!&quot; is fine. But there's no point if its just reinventing the wheel. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As it stands, a game of spy vs spy isn't limited to a cell or even an agency. In the Cold War, America and the Soviet Union were very much aware of each other, and where their borders were, yet ultimately the threat of &quot;nuclear annihilation&quot;, as someone aptly put, meant only a shadow war could be introduced. And as the World of Darkness already shows numerous times, you don't need to be a Guardian of the Veil to fight a war mortals don't know about. Mages and Werewolves cause dramatic effects all the time without the world knowing they exist--mostly because of a cleanup crew, or cosmic shinanigans. </div> </div> </div> Except Demon isn't about the US versus Soviet Union. Its about the US versus, say, North Korea. In the Cold War, the two forces of US and SU were roughly equal in power. In DtD, the power is absolutely lopsided towards the God Machine, so the demons have to act like the North Korean army and fight using guerrilla tactics.<br /> <br /> &quot;Being a demon in the World of Darkness is like being an intelligence agent deep behind enemy lines.&quot; You're not sitting behind lines at a well protected base. You're an American spy deep within Russia's heartland with unreliable backup and only a faint hope of finding your way home (Hell). Once you reach Hell, then yeah, its like you're in the US with its full military might backing you up. But that's not the default setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Spy-like? A Summer Courtier would call it an option, but not the full spectrum of what war entails. We'd be bored if everyone played spies. I know, I've <i>played</i> that game on TF2... yick. </div> </div> </div> ........ The entire basis of DtD is being a techgnostic espionage. Its the heart of the game. If your group plays DtD, yes, you will all be spies. This has nothing to do with how Changeling Courts work. This is a completely different game. Also, Winter Court is the one full of spies, not Summer. Sure, Sabatours are warriors, but Tempters, Integrators, and Inquisitors aren't.<br /> <br /> If you're not into the spy/espionage angle, that's fair enough. Its a departure from the game as written, but its simple enough to tweak things in that direction. But you have to understand that the spy thing is the game. Saying &quot;yick&quot; or that everyone would be bored makes me question if you like the game in the first place.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T13:40:33-07:00","id":604927,"title":"","content":"You're getting worked up over nothing then. If I'm wrong, my statements'll speak for themselves. If you're not here to help me play the game I'm looking for, however, leave. The Game will survive the thread's content.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":974,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","user":"MrParaduo","date":". 07-27-2015, 04:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T13:47:25-07:00","id":604941,"title":"","content":"Demon: the Descent is compared to the Cold War, not because you have two superpowers facing each other across the globe, but because <i>the two opponents never directly engaged each other in an all out war</i>. Instead, it was a state where they fight by proxies, where we fight over ideology, where success is achieved by finding out the enemy's plan and stopping it instead of soldiers killed on a battlefield. Its called the Cold War because the opponents never actually directly fought! There were proxy wars, sure, but there were no large scale operations between the two sides.<br /> <br /> There's a reason that James Bond was originally created in the era of the Cold War. That's exactly the type of thing people think of when we talk about Cold War.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T13:54:08-07:00","id":604946,"title":"","content":"Well too bad. I don't care for that restriction. Good day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T14:10:46-07:00","id":604960,"title":"","content":"Please check out person of interest. It covers pretty well how demons fight in a cold war vs a god. Demons take over or take down infrastructures to get more power to help them survive and fight. Some Gm's always leave out being its a game of espionage that other demons can be your enemy as you try to take one infrastructure maybe some others let you do the hard work and come in and try to kill you. <br /> <br /> If you want an all outfight with the god machine it could be a end game type of thing were your demons move the pieces into place to create world war 3 getting governments to help them fight the god machine with out them know that's what they are fighting. <br /> Also demons have Agencies which can be sources of great power and resources. <br /> <br /> I don't know if you can tell I really love demon and its themes. <br /> <br /> Check out this trailer <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HGb8juxyklY\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HGb8juxyklY\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HGb8juxyklY\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HGb8juxyklY </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-27T14:14:44-07:00","id":604964,"title":"","content":"It would be interesting to see what demons would be like during world war 3","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T06:01:09-07:00","id":613256,"title":"","content":"Btw, GottaGoFeast, any progress so far?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T06:47:56-07:00","id":613309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=613256#post613256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Btw, GottaGoFeast, any progress so far?</div> </div> </div> </div> I know it may seem like I am skipping around my promise because I'm posting here often as of late, but I assure you I am not. The main obstacle I'm facing right now is balancing the Rule Of Cool with minimal thematic fidelity. I'm thinking about giving numbers to that Tempter palace that MCN mentioned.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/584654-developing-demonic-infrastructure?p=604899#post604899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Without using any changes to the rules or setting, I've designed a Tempter palace for a local agency to live in comfort, as well as free to relax in their demon forms and generally free from Compromise checks, complete with stuff from Hiers to Hell, demon made cryptids, and Unchained guards armed with the best gadgets.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-08-03T06:49:07-07:00","id":613312,"title":"","content":"Fair deal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}